#question(title: [Monotonicity and concavity])[
  Let $display(f(x) = x e^(-x^2 \/ 2))$.

  + Find the intervals where $f$ is
    increasing or decreasing, and its local
    extrema.
  + Find the intervals where $f$ is concave
    up or concave down, and its inflection
    points.
  + Calculate $display(lim_(x -> oo) f(x))$
    and $display(lim_(x -> - oo) f(x))$.
  + Using this information, sketch the graph
    of $f$.
]
